    "title": "Disability discrimination complaint preceded Chicago health commissioner's exit - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rose Schmidt ,\n6 hours ago A month after Mayor Brandon Johnson asked Chicago's public health commissioner to resign, new documents reveal what preceded her departure. Less than three years after Johnson tapped Dr. Olusimbo \"Simbo\" Ige to lead the Department of Public Health, he asked for her letter of resignation. NBC 5 Investigates obtained documents showing an employee filed a complaint alleging disability discrimination. Read full article\n2",
